  "question": {
    "text": "Consider the following statements related to temperature dependence of rate constants.<br />Identify the correct statements,<br />A. The Arrhenius equation holds true only for an elementary homogenous reaction.<br />B. The unit of A is same as that of k in Arrhenius equation.<br />C. At a given temperature, a low activation energy means a fast reaction.<br />D. A and Ea as used in Arrhenius equation depend on temperature.<br />E. When $\\mathrm{Ea} \\gg \\mathrm{RT}$. A and Ea become interdependent.<br />Choose the correct answer from the options given below :",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
